# Roku — `appdimens-roku` 3.2.0

Decide intent first with `appdimens-layout-intent`. On Roku the base screen is the **1920×1080 mock-up in px**
(reference mode); use mode `"tv"` only when sharing dp tokens with Android TV / mobile (960×540 dp).
Upstream skill: `bodenberg/appdimens-roku/skills/appdimens-roku/SKILL.md`.

## Install / wire-up

Copy `source/AppDimens.brs` and `source/AppDimensTokens.brs` (+ `source/AppDimensCustom.brs` for custom strategies)
into the channel's `source/`. In every component that sizes nodes:

```xml
<script type="text/brightscript" uri="pkg:/source/AppDimens.brs" />
<script type="text/brightscript" uri="pkg:/source/AppDimensTokens.brs" />
```

```brightscript
sub init()
    ad = AppDimens()                      ' one per BrightScript context (components, Tasks)
    safe = ad.safeRect("title")
    card.translation = [safe.x, safe.y]
    card.width = ad.sdp(720)
    font.size = ad.fontSize(32)
end sub
```

## Intent → token

| Intent | Token |
|---|---|
| cards, rows, padding, focus rings | `ad.sdp(v)` |
| posters / tiles that keep a grid on any space | `ad.asdp(v)` |
| titles and labels | `ad.fontSize(v)` (integer) |
| long descriptions | `ad.fontSize(v, "logarithmic")` · `ad.logssp(v)` |
| hero art that must cover / stay whole | `ad.flsdp(v)` / `ad.ftsdp(v)` |
| focusable content / titles | inside `ad.safeRect("action")` / `ad.safeRect("title")` |
| inverters, `Px` | `ad.resolve("hdpLwa", v)`, `ad.dimen("16sdpPx")` |

## Rules

- Never hard-code HD factors (`* 0.6667`); `AppDimens()` reads `ui_resolutions` (one entry → autoscale, coordinates
  stay 1920×1080; several → the device's resolution).
- Reference mode values are already coordinates: no `Px` tokens there. Mode `"tv"`: `ad.px(ad.sdp(v))`.
- Don't put the instance in node fields; call `AppDimens()` in each `init()`.
- Custom strategies only when `customStrategies` is declared: `AppDimens_LoadStrategies(text)`,
  `ad = AppDimens_Custom()`, `ad.cdp(16, "id")` — see `appdimens-custom-strategies`.
- Verify with `npm test` (brs-engine) and `npx bsc` in appdimens-roku, and on FHD + HD devices.
